course: dictionary
lesson: 1621
title: Chess on the board
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Chess is a noun. Here it is the name of a game, and the words around it show this. «At the chess tournament Dev from another school beats Sam on time in the final.» A tournament is a competition, so chess is a game people play against each other.
explain: Look at the phrases around chess to learn more about it. «Chess club» is a group that meets to play. «Chessboard» is the board the game is played on, and a «chess piece» is one of the pieces you move on it.
explain: Some games depend on thinking and some depend on luck. «Some games are won by thinking (chess) and some by luck (a simple dice game).» Chess is a game of thinking, so the better planner usually wins, not the luckiest player.
fact: Chess is a board game for two players.
fact: The board has 64 squares, in 8 rows of 8.
fact: The pieces are kings, queens, bishops, knights, rooks and pawns.
fact: The aim is to trap the other player's king. This is called checkmate.
fact: Chess has changed over time, and the chaturanga elephant became today's bishop.
exercise: «At the chess tournament Dev from another school beats Sam on time in the final.» What is a tournament? | A type of dice | A square on the board | A kind of chess piece | *A competition where players play each other
exercise: How many squares does a chessboard have? | *64 | 16 | 32 | 100
exercise: In chess, what is the aim of the game? | *Trap the other player's king | Roll the highest number on a dice | Get your pieces off the board first | Collect the most pawns
test: Which of these is a chess piece? | Ball | Bucket | Ladder | *Rook
test: «Sam stops waiting at the table and goes to chess club, and by spring he has two new mates.» What is a chess club? | A game with dice | *A group that meets to play chess | A table for eating lunch | A shop that sells boards
exam: Jake says chess is «mid». What does mid mean in this sentence? | Very fast | *Boring, not special | A kind of chess piece | Made of wood
